<title>USA: PureTec Corp Q1 Oct 31 loss widens.</title>
<headline>PureTec Corp Q1 Oct 31 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>RIDGEFIELD, N.J. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>PureTec Corp. and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>(Dollars and shares in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     Three months ended</p>
<p>							    Oct. 31,</p>
<p>						     1996	   1995/a</p>
<p> Net sales				     $65,960	 $67,648</p>
<p> Costs and expenses			   63,121	  63,829</p>
<p> Income from operations			2,839	   3,819</p>
<p> Loss from continuing operations	 (2,753)	 (1,669)</p>
<p> Loss from discontinued operations	     0	   (206)</p>
<p> Net loss					(2,753)	 (1,875)</p>
<p> Net loss per share/b			 (0.09)	  (0.07)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding				   29,339	  27,124</p>
<p>(a)  Fiscal 1995 results have been restated to reflect the equity method of accounting for Evolutions Inc., a 42% owned affiliate as of Oct. 31, 1996.  Previously, PureTec had a majority ownership and therefore had accounted for Evolutions as a consolidated subsidiary.</p>
<p>(b)  Loss per share for the three months ended Oct. 31, 1995 is calculated after accounting for a $126 increase in value of redeemable preferred stock.  The redeemable preferred was converted to common stock on July 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
